{
  "description": "Sending and managing email. Live responses (2026-10-29) and resend-node disagree with the spec: getEmail and listEmails return `bcc`, `cc` and `reply_to` as null when unset, `message_id` as null while an email is scheduled, and always carry `scheduled_at`; getEmail also returns `tags`. resend-node types `html`, `text` and `topic_id` as nullable too. PATCH /emails/{email_id} takes `scheduled_at` in the body (the spec declares none, so the SDK could not reschedule) and, like cancelEmail, returns `{ object, id }`, not the request options or the full email. A permissive batch (`x-batch-validation: permissive`) returns the rejected items in `errors`. getEmailMetrics rows carry each requested metric beside the dimension columns, as resend-node's `EmailMetricsDataRow` types them. Response members are narrowed to what Resend returns: required where resend-node, the maintained official SDK, declares them non-optional and every live response (2026-10-29) carried them, and nullable where resend-node allows null or a live response held null. An email that is no longer scheduled can't be rescheduled or canceled (EmailNotScheduled). Errors on these operations match Resend's error `name` and status; the classes shared with other areas are in shared.json.",
